# Working specs and plans — local agent working context, not part of the submission
#
# `docs/` (a bare directory pattern) excludes the directory itself, and git
# never descends into an excluded directory to evaluate further rules — so no
# negation of a path underneath it can ever re-include anything (this was
# tried and confirmed not to work: `git check-ignore` kept reporting files
# under docs/submission/ as ignored by the `docs/` line even with
# `!docs/submission/` and `!docs/submission/**` both present). `docs/*`
# instead excludes only docs' direct children, which git does still descend
# into, so the negation below actually takes effect.
docs/*
!docs/submission/

